    "body": "FWIW ES6 changed a bunch of error classes, and I don't remember any compatibility reports in Chrome from that specifically. The extremely coarse error classes are just not very useful...\r\n\r\nNote that we have lots more enum-style things in ECMA-402, and we like to throw RangeError. See https://tc39.github.io/ecma402/#sec-getoption",
